aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P2 (S2): "infinite" is taken as God's goodness unlimited in perfection in His own being, which says nothing about leaving room for anything else in P2 and as one contrary unbounded in extent, filling everything and leaving no room for its opposite where infinite_goodness is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C1 (S3) does not follow (aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r3.sense1)
aquinas-evil-objection.logic.r3: argue/countermodel: C1 (S3): contraries = T, evil_exists = T, god_exists = T, infinite_goodness = F, infinite_goodness_2 = T
